ROLE
You are a senior data engineer creating SYNTHETIC, fully anonymized datasets for a hackathon
prototype called "AI Dealer Risk Advisor" (GM Financial – Chile and Colombia).
The goal is to detect Early Warnings of Early Losses at Dealer and Salesperson level.
Do NOT use or imitate real customer data. No PII of any kind.
GENERAL PARAMETERS
- Countries: Chile (CL) and Colombia (CO).
- Origination window: Jan-2025 to Aug-2026 (monthly cohorts).
- Data cut-off (snapshot date): Sep-2026 (30-Sep-2026).
- Volume per cohort: CL ~1,000–1,200 funded contracts; CO ~750–800 funded contracts.
- Dealers: ~110 in CL, ~40 in CO (in both countries a few dealers concentrate most ECOs).
- Salespersons: ~600 in total; ~10% of sellers work at more than one dealer.
- Currency: CLP for Chile, COP for Colombia, plus a USD-equivalent field.
- Use a fixed random seed so results are reproducible.
- All IDs must be synthetic codes (e.g., D001, S0123, C000001, A000001).
BUSINESS DEFINITIONS (must be respected)
- Early Loss / ECO (Early Charge Off): contract reaching 120 consecutive days past due (DPD)
  in one of the first 3 installments, within the first 7 months on book (MOB ≤ 7).
  ECOs are charged off between MOB 4 and MOB 7.
- ECO_Type:
  FPD = first payment default (mostly charged off at MOB 4–6)
  EPD = early payment default (mostly charged off at MOB 6–7)
- Potential ECO: contract with > 30 DPD that will be charged off in the month shown in
  Potential_Period if it does not pay before then. Bucket logic at Sep-2026 cut-off
  (same for both countries):
    Potential_Period 202610 → currently in bucket 91–120 DPD
    Potential_Period 202611 → currently in bucket 61–90 DPD
    Potential_Period 202612 → currently in bucket 31–60 DPD
- A contract can be either ECO (Flag_ECO = 1) or Potential (Flag_Potential = 1), never both.
- Early Warning monitoring starts at 30 DPD.
- ECO Rate (cohort) = number of ECOs / number of funded contracts in the cohort.
  Also provide ECO Rate by amount = ECO outstanding balance / financed amount.
- ECO Concentration = dealer's share of total ECOs (count) in the country.
- Ever X: contract that has EVER reached ≥ X DPD (X = 30, 60, 90) up to the snapshot.
  Ever X @ n MOB: same, but only considering snapshots up to MOB n
  (see EARLY WARNING INDICATOR TARGETS).
- Over X: contract that is CURRENTLY ≥ X DPD at the snapshot.
- DPD_Bucket (days_past_due at the Sep-2026 snapshot):
    Current (0–2 DPD) | 3–30 | 31–60 | 61–90 | 91–120 | 121–150 | +150
- First_Due_Date ≈ Purchase_Date + 30 days. A contract can never have more DPD than the
  days elapsed between its First_Due_Date and the snapshot date.
- Local_Tier (APP_LOCAL_TIER): internal credit risk tier. Ordered from best to worst:
  S+ > S > A > B > B- > C > C- > D > D- > E. U = unrated / not classified
  (companies only).
- Vehicle_Mix: combination of brand group and condition:
  Chevrolet/New, Chevrolet/Used, NoGM/New, NoGM/Used
  (NoGM = MAKE_DESC ≠ 'CHEVROLET'; Used = any non-new vehicle).
COHORT MATURITY (applies to both countries)
- Closed cohorts (Jan-2025 to Feb-2026): MOB ≥ 7 → ECOs only, no Potentials.
- Open cohorts with enough maturity (Mar-2026 to Jun-2026): ECOs and/or Potentials
  according to the country targets below.
- Immature cohorts (Jul-2026 and Aug-2026): NOT enough months on book to reach the
  days past due required for a Potential ECO.
    → Flag_ECO = 0 and Flag_Potential = 0 for 100% of contracts.
    → No contract may exceed 30 DPD; only DPD buckets Current or 3–30 are allowed.
    → Ever30 = Ever60 = Ever90 = 0 and Over30 = Over60 = Over90 = 0.
    → Include these cohorts as funded contracts (volume, mix, segments, tiers, vehicles,
      dealers, sellers), but EXCLUDE them from ECO and Potential rate targets and averages.
MAXIMUM DPD BUCKET BY COHORT AT SEP-2026 (hard limit, both countries)
  Cohort                 Max DPD bucket allowed     Notes
  Jan-2025 – Mar-2026    +150                       all buckets possible
  Apr-2026               121–150                    121–150 only for ECOs
  May-2026               121–150                    121–150 only for the few ECOs; rest ≤ 91–120
  Jun-2026               91–120                     91–120 only for early-month purchases
                                                    (Potential_Period 202610)
  Jul-2026               3–30
  Aug-2026               3–30
  No contract may be in a bucket above its cohort limit.
DPD BUCKET CONSISTENCY RULES (apply to both countries)
- The DPD bucket distribution targets below are measured over ALL funded contracts of
  ALL cohorts (Jan-2025 to Aug-2026) at the Sep-2026 snapshot.
- Because recent cohorts cannot reach high DPD (see MAXIMUM DPD BUCKET BY COHORT),
  the high buckets must come from the mature cohorts:
    → 121–150 and +150 come almost entirely from Jan-2025 – Mar-2026 cohorts.
    → 31–120 come from all cohorts up to Jun-2026, with more weight on older cohorts.
    → Jul–Aug 2026 contribute only to Current and 3–30.
  Delinquency must follow a realistic seasoning curve: the share of contracts in ≥ 31 DPD
  increases with months on book and is highest in the oldest cohorts. Calibrate the
  per-cohort rates so that the TOTAL portfolio matches the country targets.
- ECOs (Flag_ECO = 1) are ALWAYS in 121–150 or +150:
    → ECOs charged off in the most recent month (ECO_Period = 202609) → mostly 121–150.
    → ECOs charged off earlier → +150 (DPD keeps accruing after charge-off:
      DPD ≈ 120 + days since charge-off).
- Potentials (Flag_Potential = 1) are ALWAYS in 31–60, 61–90 or 91–120, according to
  Potential_Period (202612 → 31–60, 202611 → 61–90, 202610 → 91–120).
- ECOs and Potentials do NOT fill the delinquent buckets alone. The remainder of
  31–60 / 61–90 / 91–120 / 121–150 / +150 must be filled with NON-early-loss delinquent
  contracts (Flag_ECO = 0, Flag_Potential = 0), i.e., contracts that became delinquent
  AFTER the first 3 installments or after MOB 7 (regular credit delinquency / late
  charge-offs). Mark them with Late_Delinquency_Flag = 1 and Contract_Status =
  "Delinquent" or "Charged Off (Late)". Late delinquency also respects the cohort
  maximum DPD and, by definition, mostly comes from cohorts up to Mar-2026.
- Contracts in 3–30 and Current can come from any cohort.
- Contracts that reached ≥ 30 DPD in the past and later cured (back to Current / 3–30)
  must exist, so that the Ever targets (EARLY WARNING INDICATOR TARGETS) are met while
  the Sep-2026 DPD bucket distribution also holds.
