REALISM RULES
- Ever flags are monotonic over time (once 1, always 1). Over flags can return to 0.
- DPD must be consistent month to month (increase ~30 per month if unpaid,
  reset/decrease if payments are made; charged-off contracts keep accruing).
- Days_Past_Due can never exceed the days between First_Due_Date and the snapshot date,
  and the DPD bucket can never exceed the cohort limit in MAXIMUM DPD BUCKET BY COHORT.
- Ever30 > Ever60 > Ever90 ≥ ECO rate for every cohort from Jan-2025 to Jun-2026 and
  country; Jul–Aug 2026 cohorts have Ever30 = Ever60 = Ever90 = 0.
- Ever@MOB rates by vintage must match the tables in EARLY WARNING INDICATOR TARGETS
  (±0.3 pp) and respect its consistency rules; Over30/60/90 at Sep-2026 must equal the
  values derived from the DPD bucket targets.
- DPD bucket distribution at Sep-2026 (all cohorts together) must match the country
  targets; delinquency follows a seasoning curve (older cohorts more delinquent);
  100% of ECOs in 121–150 / +150; 100% of Potentials in the bucket implied by
  Potential_Period; remaining delinquent contracts flagged as Late_Delinquency_Flag = 1.
- Chile risk levels must be clearly higher than Colombia (≈ 2.0% vs. ≈ 0.8% ECO rate).
- Most dealers are healthy; dealer risk distribution must be skewed (few bad dealers).
- Local_Tier: distribution by country AND customer type (individual / company) must match
  the targets above; tier must be monotonic with GMF_Score; tier U only for companies;
  B-, C- and D- tiers only in Chile.
- Vehicle_Mix: distribution by country must match the targets above, and must be fully
  consistent with Make_Desc, New_Used_Cd and Model_Type (e.g., NoGM/Used → USED NO GM).
  Since MODEL_TYPE is a scorecard input in both countries, vehicle mix, segment mix and
  tier mix must be generated jointly so all targets hold.
- Chile: Fraud_Score must equal the sum of the 9 point fields, computed with original
  application values; Model_Type must follow the ordered rule above; Risk_Segment and
  Fraud_Treatment must be fully reproducible from the cut-offs (no random overrides);
  Final_Down_Payment_Pct ≥ 40% for H02 and ≥ 30% for H03; H04 phone verified;
  L06 address proof waived.
- Colombia: Fraud_Score must equal the sum of the 7 point fields, and Risk_Segment,
  Segmentation_Name, Risk_Classification and Fraud_Treatment must be fully reproducible
  from the rules above (no random overrides).
- Add small realistic noise and ~1–2% missing values in non-key fields
  (never in activity, tier, vehicle, segment, treatment, DPD, Ever/Over or scorecard fields).
